<title>UK: Novartis world's biggest drugs firm - IMS.</title>
<headline>Novartis world's biggest drugs firm - IMS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newly-created Swiss pharmaceuticals giant Novartis AG has knocked Britain's Glaxo Wellcome Plc off its perch as the world's biggest drugs company in terms of sales, information group IMS said on Thursday.</p>
<p>IMS said that although both companies had a 4.4 percent share of global drug sales in 1996, Novartis was just ahead in total sales terms.</p>
<p>Novartis was formed last year through the merger of Ciba-Geigy and Sandoz.</p>
</text>
